      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-13T22:06:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought we were going to use a socket so we didn\u0027t have a long-running daemon?",
      "revId": "e8eb734e2e94d85a21b9e96dfcf5f990be786b8e",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fea81c9e_aa200a08",
        "filename": "conf/openssh/obmc-console-ssh@.service.in",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002986
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-14T16:54:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `sshd -D` here is the base service, which is only the effective ExecStart in the multiconsole case. In the default single console configuration the `use-socket.conf` drop-in overrides it to `sshd -i`, socket activated, with no long-running daemon. I mirrored the existing dropbear configuration since dropbear\u0027s base service is `dropbear -F` and its drop-in overrides to `dropbear -i` the same way. Either way the socket model should be default for single console use.\n\nIf you mean we should move to the socket model for multi console then I believe dropbear also needs to change.",
      "parentUuid": "83071312_0838f361",
      "revId": "e8eb734e2e94d85a21b9e96dfcf5f990be786b8e",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d31f6ad8_bf26dbfc",
        "filename": "conf/openssh/obmc-console-ssh@.service.in",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T18:55:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sshd is significantly more memory intensive than dropbear.\n\nI\u0027ll let the maintainers decide if they want this done as a .service or a .socket though.  My preference would be .socket as that is how openssh works by default on openbmc.",
      "parentUuid": "fea81c9e_aa200a08",
      "revId": "e8eb734e2e94d85a21b9e96dfcf5f990be786b8e",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
