      "writtenOn": "2026-07-13T22:06:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we make `ssh` an option which is [\"none\", \"dropbear\", \"ssh\"] instead of 2 different options?",
      "revId": "e8eb734e2e94d85a21b9e96dfcf5f990be786b8e",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc895103_db5e63b1",
        "filename": "meson.build",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002986
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-14T16:54:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like this idea; might be breaking changes if `ssh` is already being used as a bool flag in scripts elsewhere, though. If that\u0027s a concern then we could make it an enum like this `[\u0027auto\u0027, \u0027disabled\u0027, \u0027enabled\u0027, \u0027dropbear\u0027, \u0027openssh\u0027]`. I think the ssh option originally had \u0027auto\u0027, \u0027disabled\u0027, and \u0027enabled\u0027 so these will need to be mapped.",
      "parentUuid": "b8558c2d_707e1701",
      "revId": "e8eb734e2e94d85a21b9e96dfcf5f990be786b8e",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ef9eec6_9981cfac",
        "filename": "meson.build",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T18:55:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "auto/disabled/enabled are a concept in meson of a \"feature\".  That should not be replicated here.\n\ndisabled / enabled are hard settings.\nauto essentially means \"enable if all the dependencies are met\".",
      "parentUuid": "fc895103_db5e63b1",
      "revId": "e8eb734e2e94d85a21b9e96dfcf5f990be786b8e",
